28. Docker save/load & export/import
Docker save

Used to save Docker image into tar file
Includes layers + metadata + history
Used for backup / transfer

✅ Command:
docker save -o image.tar nginx
✅ One-line:
Save converts a Docker image into a tar file with full layers and history.

Docker load

Used to load image from tar file into Docker
Restores full image with layers
Opposite of save

✅ Command:
docker load -i image.tar
✅ One-line:
Load restores a Docker image from a tar file.

Docker export

Used to export container filesystem into tar
Includes only container data (no layers/history)
Lightweight

✅ Command:
docker export mycontainer -o container.tar
✅ One-line:
Export saves a container filesystem as a tar without image history.

Docker import

Used to create image from tar file
No history/layers (flat image)
Opposite of export

✅ Command:
docker import container.tar myimage:latest
✅ One-line:
Import creates a Docker image from a container tar file.

✅ ✅ Important Interview Difference

save / load → image (with layers ✅)
export / import → container (no layers ❌)
